  "body": "<p>The sixth time was the charm for Elise Mertens in her rivalry with Coco Gauff.</p>\n<p>No. 13 seed Mertens defeated No. 3 seed Gauff for the first time 6-3, 6-3 in the China Open fourth round, advancing to her first Beijing quarterfinal in her seventh appearance.</p>\n<p>Despite trailing 0-5 in their head-to-head prior to Wednesday, Mertens had come close to beating Gauff before. In their first meeting, she led the then 17-year-old 6-0, 3-1 in the 2021 Eastbourne first round before falling 0-6, 7-6(4), 7-5. Eight months ago, she held three match points on Gauff in the Dubai third round, only for the American to escape 2-6, 7-6(9), 6-3.</p>\n<p>This time, Mertens held on in impressive style, winning 10 of her last 11 service points and sealing victory with her second ace -- ironically, her first straightforward scoreline of the tournament so far. In the second round, she led Katie Volynets 6-0, 3-0 but ultimately needed to come from a break down in the decider to win 6-0, 4-6, 7-5 in 2 hours and 54 minutes. In the third round, she overturned a 2-0 third-set deficit to quell Jelena Ostapenko 6-2, 3-6, 6-4.</p>\n<p>After sealing the win over Gauff, she revealed she had some extra motivation -- though it was more about romance than revenge.</p>\n<p>\"My coach/boyfriend [Christopher Heyman], it's his birthday tomorrow,\" she said in her on-court interview. \"So for me, this win is dedicated to him.\"</p><div class=\"articleWidget center\">\n        <aside class=\"instagram-post embeddable-widget embeddable-widget--floating embeddable-widget--centered-mobile \"><blockquote class=\"instagram-media\" data-instgrm-captioned data-instgrm-permalink=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DeL4yMrgXV6/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading\" data-instgrm-version=\"14\" style=\" background:#FFF; border:0; border-radius:3px; box-shadow:0 0 1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.5),0 1px 10px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.15); margin: 1px; max-width:540px; min-width:326px; padding:0; width:99.375%; wid